out would build the same surface twice and add an artificial serialization edge, so it is covered by the single comparison-view epic at the higher priority (P0). The strategy itself notes the requirements were consolidated from two customer councils with overlapping wording kept. |\n| HLR-4 | P2 | E004 | Documentation of the comparison workflow from both entry points (runs list and registry). Docs-authoring priority derived from strategy priority Major → P1 per the docs-authoring priority exception. |\n\nAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n1. **Missing strategy sections.** The strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n   Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then Acceptance Criteria, and no\n   Non-Functional Requirements; the Affected Components section is a bare list\n   without change descriptions or owner teams. Epic ACs were therefore derived\n   from the HLRs, and owner teams were inferred from the architecture-context\n   \"Owning team\" fields (Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard, Model Registry → Model\n   Registry, Data Science Pipelines → RHOAI Pipelines). The docs epic's team\n   (RHOAI Docs) is a convention-based inference — Documentation has no\n   architecture-context file. Verify team assignments at refinement.\n2. **\"Training runs\" surface assumption (scope trap).** The problem statement\n   and HLR-1 speak of \"training and pipeline runs\", but Training Operator is\n   not an affected component and the platform's runs surface is Data Science\n   Pipelines. The decomposition assumes training runs are executed (or\n   otherwise surfaced) as pipeline runs in the existing runs list. This is\n   captured as a verification acceptance criterion on E001 rather than an\n   Investigation epic: the strategy's affected-components list implies no\n   Training Operator work exists, and the answer does not change which epics\n   exist — it would only expand E001's scope. If training runs turn out to\n   surface through a different path, re-scope E001 before implementation.\n3. **Passive component — Data Science Pipelines.** No code changes are\n   expected there: run parameters and metrics are already served through the\n   existing KFP v2 surfaces the Dashboard consumes. Validation that\n   pipeline-run parameters/metrics are complete enough for side-by-side\n   comparison and diff highlighting is folded into E001's acceptance criteria.\n4. **No priority inversions detected.** E001 is the only P0 epic and has no\n   dependencies; nothing P1/P2 blocks it. HLR-3's P1 label does not push a\n   split (see traceability row above).\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nNot applicable — the strategy has no external dependencies with uncertain\ntiming; all work is in-platform. E001 (P0) delivers standalone user value\n(run comparison from the runs list) independent of the registry-linkage work\n(E002/E003, P1).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":28430,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b06abf3d2c8b643","agent_id":"ac7da890a996a8d3d","session_id":"baae94b6-b5f6-4a75-a782-f5328e436f6d","uuid":"6405ccb5-0b87-4501-a4db-9199a401ca64","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:22:15.568Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9015"}
