{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8f932488621e444","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n3\tepic_count: 4\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9015: Experiment comparison for training and pipeline runs\n11\t\n12\tStrategy status: Refinement Done. Strategy priority: Major. The strategy was not\n13\ttriaged in Step 0: it spans three components (Dashboard, Model Registry, Data\n14\tScience Pipelines) and multiple architecturally distinct work streams (Dashboard\n15\tUI, Model Registry backend metadata, documentation authoring), so the\n16\tbelow-threshold path does not apply, and code changes are required, so the\n17\tdocs-only path does not apply either.\n18\t\n19\t## Epic List\n20\t\n21\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n22\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n23\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E001 | Run comparison view: side-by-side parameters and metrics with diff highlighting | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n24\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E002 | Link registered model versions to the runs that produced them | Implementation | Model Registry | P1 |\n25\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E003 | Open a run comparison from the Model Registry | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n26\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E004 | Document the run comparison workflow | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Docs | P1 |\n27\t\n28\t## Dependency DAG\n29\t\n30\t```mermaid\n31\tgraph TD\n32\t    E001[\"RHAISTRAT-9015-E001 Run comparison view\"] --> E003[\"RHAISTRAT-9015-E003 Registry entry point\"]\n33\t    E002[\"RHAISTRAT-9015-E002 Run linkage on model versions\"] --> E003\n34\t    E001 --> E004[\"RHAISTRAT-9015-E004 Documentation\"]\n35\t    E002 --> E004\n36\t    E003 --> E004\n37\t```\n38\t\n39\tArrows point from dependency to dependent (the epic at the arrow's tail must\n40\tcomplete before the epic at the head starts).\n41\t\n42\t## DAG Justification\n43\t\n44\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n45\t|------|------|-----------|\n46\t| E001 ∥ E002 (no edge) | Rule 14 | Different components and repos (odh-dashboard vs model-registry), no shared artifacts — the comparison view and the run-reference metadata can be built independently. |\n47\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 12/13 (framework/surface → consumer) | The registry entry point's code opens and pre-populates the run comparison view; it builds against that UI surface and cannot be implemented or verified before the comparison view exists. |\n48\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The registry entry point consumes the run reference stored on registered model versions and served through the Model Registry REST API — an API artifact another epic's code builds against. |\n49\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation must describe the comparison workflow as built. |\n50\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation covers the registry-side linkage semantics as built. |\n51\t| E003 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation covers the registry entry point to the comparison as built. |\n52\t\n53\tNo konflux-onboarding, repo-onboarding, or license-validation epics are needed:\n54\tall three affected components are already in the platform and Konflux-onboarded\n55\tper architecture context, and no new component is introduced.\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n58\t\n59\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n60\t|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n61\t| HLR-1 | P0 | E001 | Side-by-side comparison of parameters and metrics for two or more selected runs. |\n62\t| HLR-2 | P1 | E002, E003 | Split along the component/team boundary: E002 (Model Registry team) stores and serves the run reference on model versions; E003 (RHOAI Dashboard team) adds the registry-UI entry point that opens a comparison. Both halves are needed to satisfy the HLR. |\n63\t| HLR-3 | P1 | E001 (consolidated with HLR-1) | The \"diff\" view is a presentation mode of the same comparison surface over the same run data — same component, same team, same UI surface. Splitting it out would build the same surface twice and add an artificial serialization edge, so it is covered by the single comparison-view epic at the higher priority (P0). The strategy itself notes the requirements were consolidated from two customer councils with overlapping wording kept. |\n64\t| HLR-4 | P2 | E004 | Documentation of the comparison workflow from both entry points (runs list and registry). Docs-authoring priority derived from strategy priority Major → P1 per the docs-authoring priority exception. |\n65\t\n66\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n67\t\n68\t## Health Warnings\n69\t\n70\t1. **Missing strategy sections.** The strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n71\t   Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then Acceptance Criteria, and no\n72\t   Non-Functional Requirements; the Affected Components section is a bare list\n73\t   without change descriptions or owner teams. Epic ACs were therefore derived\n74\t   from the HLRs, and owner teams were inferred from the architecture-context\n75\t   \"Owning team\" fields (Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard, Model Registry → Model\n76\t   Registry, Data Science Pipelines → RHOAI Pipelines). The docs epic's team\n77\t   (RHOAI Docs) is a convention-based inference — Documentation has no\n78\t   architecture-context file. Verify team assignments at refinement.\n79\t2. **\"Training runs\" surface assumption (scope trap).** The problem statement\n80\t   and HLR-1 speak of \"training and pipeline runs\", but Training Operator is\n81\t   not an affected component and the platform's runs surface is Data Science\n82\t   Pipelines. The decomposition assumes training runs are executed (or\n83\t   otherwise surfaced) as pipeline runs in the existing runs list. This is\n84\t   captured as a verification acceptance criterion on E001 rather than an\n85\t   Investigation epic: the strategy's affected-components list implies no\n86\t   Training Operator work exists, and the answer does not change which epics\n87\t   exist — it would only expand E001's scope. If training runs turn out to\n88\t   surface through a different path, re-scope E001 before implementation.\n89\t3. **Passive component — Data Science Pipelines.** No code changes are\n90\t   expected there: run parameters and metrics are already served through the\n91\t   existing KFP v2 surfaces the Dashboard consumes. Validation that\n92\t   pipeline-run parameters/metrics are complete enough for side-by-side\n93\t   comparison and diff highlighting is folded into E001's acceptance criteria.\n94\t4. **No priority inversions detected.** E001 is the only P0 epic and has no\n95\t   dependencies; nothing P1/P2 blocks it. HLR-3's P1 label does not push a\n96\t   split (see traceability row above).\n97\t\n98\t## Tiered Delivery\n99\t\n100\tNot applicable — the strategy has no external dependencies with uncertain\n101\ttiming; all work is in-platform. E001 (P0) delivers standalone user value\n102\t(run comparison from the runs list) independent of the registry-linkage work\n103\t(E002/E003, P1).\n104\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2817a4c36d37510","agent_id":"a06690004f4f28428","session_id":"baae94b6-b5f6-4a75-a782-f5328e436f6d","uuid":"c18258c0-9821-42d6-ba8d-b16b645a17cf","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:24:00.452Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8f932488621e444","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
