{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e9744210a2bdaf3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9015-E002\n3\ttitle: Link registered model versions to the runs that produced them\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n5\tcomponent: Model Registry\n6\tteam: Model Registry\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Link registered model versions to the runs that produced them\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tRegistered model versions record a reference to the run (training or pipeline)\n34\tthat produced them, stored and served by the Model Registry. This lineage link\n35\tis what lets a comparison be opened starting from a registered model version,\n36\tsupporting model promotion decisions with traceability back to the producing\n37\texperiment.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Define and store a run reference on registered model versions, using the\n42\t  Model Registry's existing metadata extension point for structured metadata\n43\t  on ModelVersion entities (custom properties) rather than a new schema\n44\t  object.\n45\t- Expose the run reference through the Model Registry REST API so Dashboard\n46\t  surfaces and API consumers can read it.\n47\t- Keep the link optional and backward compatible: registration without a run\n48\t  reference remains fully supported.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- Given a model version registered with knowledge of its producing run, the\n53\t  run reference is stored on the model version and retrievable through the\n54\t  Model Registry REST API.\n55\t- Model versions created without a run reference continue to be created,\n56\t  listed, served, and deployed without error, and existing model versions are\n57\t  not migrated or altered.\n58\t- The run reference round-trips through the documented API surface (written at\n59\t  registration, read back unchanged).\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- **HLR-2 (P1, data side)** — registered model versions link back to the run\n64\t  that produced them. The registry-UI entry point that consumes this link is\n65\t  tracked separately within the Dashboard component.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2817a4c36d37510","agent_id":"a06690004f4f28428","session_id":"baae94b6-b5f6-4a75-a782-f5328e436f6d","uuid":"a50d3e56-2be0-4d18-974a-5136aedcba7b","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:24:03.221Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e9744210a2bdaf3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
