{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4a926a246615051","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9015\n3\tscore: 14\n4\tpass: true\n5\trecommendation: accept\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: minor\n8\t  criterion: AI Implementability Scoring\n9\t  description: 'E001 scores human_process_gates: 0 while its own rationale states\n10\t    no approval step exists (\"ordinary team process, not a strategy-mandated gate\"),\n11\t    and E002 scores the same condition +1; per the rubric (+1 = no human approval\n12\t    step) E001 should be +1'\n13\terror: null\n14\t---\n15\t## Review Summary\n16\t\n17\tScore: 14/14 — pass\n18\tRecommendation: accept\n19\t\n20\tContract validator: OK (no violations). Triage: null — full decomposition with 4\n21\tepics, so the multi-epic shape is expected (Step 1.5 does not apply).\n22\t\n23\t## Criterion Details\n24\t\n25\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n26\t\n27\tAll four HLRs are mapped and traceable: HLR-1 (P0) → E001; HLR-2 (P1) → E002\n28\t(Model Registry backend) + E003 (Dashboard registry-UI entry point), split\n29\talong the component/team boundary with both halves recorded in the matrix;\n30\tHLR-3 (P1) → E001; HLR-4 (P2) → E004. HLR-3's consolidation into E001 is the\n31\tcorrect shape per the presentation-mode rule: the diff view is a thin increment\n32\ton E001's comparison surface (same component, same team, same run data), so a\n33\tseparate epic would be a duplication split. The bundling decision is on the\n34\trecord in both the summary's matrix row and E001's HLR Traceability section,\n35\twith rationale — compliant with the bundling-recording check. Priority\n36\tinheritment is clean: E001 is the only P0 epic and has no dependencies; nothing\n37\tP1/P2 blocks P0 work. E004 (docs-authoring) derives P1 from strategy priority\n38\tMajor per the docs-authoring exception. No priority collapse: the only\n39\tlower-priority HLR bundled upward (HLR-3) shares the implementation surface\n40\twith the P0 work, which is explicitly not a collapse.\n41\t\n42\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n43\t\n44\tThe diagram (dependency → dependent) matches frontmatter exactly: E003 depends\n45\ton [E001, E002], E004 on [E001, E002, E003], E001 and E002 have no\n46\tdependencies. No cycles, no invalid references. Every edge is justified in the\n47\tDAG Justification table: E001 → E003 is a build-against edge (the entry\n48\tpoint's code opens and pre-populates the comparison view, Rule 12/13); E002 →\n49\tE003 consumes the run reference served through the Model Registry REST API\n50\t(build-against artifact, Rule 13 — a genuine API artifact, not a build-pipeline\n51\toutput consumed as content); the three edges into E004 are Rule 11 docs-last\n52\tedges, which do not trigger priority inheritance. E001 ∥ E002 parallelism is\n53\tpreserved (different repos, no shared artifacts). No konflux-onboarding /\n54\trepo-onboarding / license-validation epics exist, and the summary's claim that\n55\tall three affected components are already in the platform and Konflux-onboarded\n56\tis corroborated by the architecture-context files (all three list \"Konflux\n57\tonboarded: yes\"). Critical path length 3 fits the M-standard heuristic (3-4).\n58\tNo conditional branch files exist, and none are needed (strategy lists no open\n59\tquestions or bounded outcomes). Cross-check of epic content found no\n60\tuncaptured data/artifact dependencies.\n61\t\n62\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n63\t\n64\tComponent/team tuples are distinct and separate: E001/E003 (Dashboard / RHOAI\n65\tDashboard), E002 (Model Registry / Model Registry), E004 (Documentation / RHOAI\n66\tDocs, docs-authoring). Teams match the architecture-context \"Owning team\"\n67\tfields (Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard, Model Registry → Model Registry); the\n68\tRHOAI Docs assignment is a convention-based inference, correctly flagged in\n69\tHealth Warnings for verification. No scope duplication: E001 (comparison view\n70\ton