ores `human_process_gates: 0` while its own rationale states no approval\n101\tstep exists and E002 scores the same condition +1 — recorded as a minor issue;\n102\ta single minor does not reduce the score.\n103\t\n104\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n105\t\n106\tEvery epic has concrete, testable Given/When/Then-style ACs derived from the\n107\tHLRs. E002 has backward-compatibility ACs (registration without a run\n108\treference keeps working; no migration of existing versions). E003 has the\n109\tgraceful-degradation AC for model versions without a run reference. E004\n110\t(docs-authoring) carries the rule-mandated technical-review AC. No konflux\n111\tchain exists, so no build-pipeline AC is required; no replacement epic exists,\n112\tso no rollback/feature-flag AC is required. No externally-controlled\n113\tpreconditions (schedule, procurement, access grants) are misfiled as ACs. No\n114\tepic body references sibling epics by draft ID.\n115\t\n116\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n117\t\n118\tThe full strategy scope is covered: side-by-side comparison (E001), diff\n119\thighlighting (E001), registry run linkage (E002/E003), documentation from both\n120\tentry points (E004). Out-of-scope boundaries are respected and carried into\n121\tE004's scope (out-of-scope features must not be documented as available).\n122\tData Science Pipelines is listed as an affected component but has no\n123\tHLR-driven code change; the decomposition treats it as passive with an\n124\texplicit Health Warning and folds the validation into E001's ACs — recorded,\n125\tnot silently dropped. The strategy's note about consolidated customer-council\n126\trequirements is carried into the traceability rationale for HLR-3. Strategy\n127\thas no open questions and no conditional outcomes, so no branches are needed.\n128\tThe strategy has no Prerequisites & Process Gates section (flagged in Health\n129\tWarnings), but HLR-4 explicitly requires documentation and E004 satisfies\n130\tRule 11.\n131\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-96e551ad022eb1be","agent_id":"ac71caae19aa21601","session_id":"baae94b6-b5f6-4a75-a782-f5328e436f6d","uuid":"358bc1d9-5aab-479c-8bbf-cf1dcb72dd0c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:27:08.119Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4a926a246615051","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
